    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "2000247245158117384",
      "url": "https://x.com/WJGBalderama/status/2000247245158117384",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/WJGBalderama/status/2000247245158117384",
      "text": "I didn’t come across Gabriel Go through an official MMDA press release or a polished government feature. I noticed him through the unfiltered lens of vlogger Dada Koo—where traffic isn’t sanitized, angles aren’t flattering, and reality has nowhere to hide.\n\nIn Dada Coo’s videos, Metro Manila reveals itself as it truly is: messy, impatient, flooded, choking, and relentlessly alive. And somewhere in that chaos, Gabriel Go keeps showing up—not as a talking head, but as a worker. No grandstanding, no microphone, no rehearsed lines. Just presence. Just action.\n\nWhile others are content to supervise from a distance, Gabriel is there in the heat, the rain, the noise—coordinating, correcting, clearing, adjusting in real time. Through Dada Coo’s camera, it becomes obvious that he understands traffic not as a spreadsheet problem, but as lived experience. You see it in how he listens to enforcers on the ground, how he reacts quickly when a plan doesn’t work, how he treats congestion as an urgent, solvable problem rather than an excuse.\n\nWhat makes this even more compelling is that this wasn’t staged. Vloggers don’t edit in competence. They capture it—or they don’t. And repeatedly, across ordinary days and ordinary crises, Gabriel Go passes that test.\n\nIn an agency often defined by press conferences and personalities, Gabriel stands out precisely because he isn’t performing for the camera. Ironically, it took a camera—Dada Koo’s—to reveal that kind of quiet professionalism.\n\nSometimes, the most credible endorsements don’t come from officials or speeches. They come from someone walking the streets with a camera, showing you who actually shows up when Metro Manila needs order in the middle of chaos. And through that lens, a 'no-frills' man of action in the person of Gabriel Go emerges.  @MMDA",
