      "text": "🌾 @pixels_online WEEKLY RECAP | Dec 07–13\n\n📉 Price Action (Dec 7–14)\n\n$PIXEL opened around $0.0106 on Dec 7 amid low volatility and trended downward throughout the week, closing near $0.0093 by Dec 14, marking a ~12% decline.\n\nDaily trading volumes averaged $60–80M, with notable peaks between Dec 10–12, while market cap slid to around $29M.\nSupport held above $0.009, reflecting broader altcoin market caution rather than project-specific weakness.\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\n🌾 NFT Market Snapshot — Farm Land by Pixels (ETH + Ronin)\n\n🌍 Farm Land NFTs recorded $13.44K in weekly volume, down 38.8%, with 33 traders participating.\n📉 Sales activity slowed, though market cap inched up to $4.88M, and the floor price rose to $547.39.\n💰 Average sale price declined to $659.34, showing reduced high-end activity despite floor stability.\n-------------------------------\n\n🐾 Pixels Pets — Ronin Network\n\n🐶 Pixels Pets NFTs posted $1.31K in volume, down 17.7%, with 53 traders active.\n📊 Market cap held steady at $66.34K, while the floor price stabilized near $14.87.\n💸 Average prices fell to $31.56, signaling quieter speculative demand.\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\n🛡️ New Hearth Modifiers (Bountyfall)\n\n🔥 Bountyfall introduced rotating Hearth Modifiers, adding fresh twists to each session.\n⚙️ Modifiers adjusted gameplay dynamically, boosting deposits, weakening sabotage, raising Hearth health, and shifting Union balance as milestones were reached.\n🕒 These Modifiers went live on Tuesday at 12:00 AM UTC, encouraging players to adapt strategies each cycle.\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\n🎉 Conference Highlights — YPS & Binance Blockchain Week\n\n🎤 At YGG Play Summit, Luke’s fireside chat filled the theater, and the Popberry Pancake Eating Contest crowned Jihoz as champion.\n💎 At Binance Blockchain Week, the Pixels booth featured exclusive merch, veggie plushies, and interactive games, drawing strong foot traffic.\n👾 Pixels also brought the Neon Zone to life in Manila, blending IRL mini-games, themed drinks, prizes, and community energy.\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\n📊 AMA Recap — Key Takeaways\n\n🛠️ The team confirmed a strong building phase, focusing on backend upgrades and new products like Stacked and Chubkins.\n🌍 Growth plans shifted toward blending Web2 user acquisition with Web3 systems, targeting mass onboarding.\n🐾 A major animal care overhaul was confirmed, larger than originally planned.\n✨ Improving new-user experience, UI, and onboarding simplicity remained a top priority.\n📱 Stacked was positioned as a core ecosystem hub, supporting staking, rewards, offers, and stronger bot resistance.\n🤖 Bot prevention focused on smart reward systems, A/B testing, and offer-based incentives.\n💎 $vPIXEL utility was set to expand, with future marketplace possibilities and broader staking integrations.\n🎄 A low-key, recurring holiday event was confirmed, alongside continued Bountyfall and Dungeon integrations.\n🔮 Long term, Pixels leaned into Web3 strengths like ownership and ecosystem design rather than competing directly with Web2 studios.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------\n\n⚡ Avrenim’s Birthday Energy Party\n\n🎉 Avrenim’s Birthday Energy Party took place on Dec 10 at the Drunken Goose, with the celebration streamed live on Twitch.\n-----------------------------\n\n🎟️ Moku’s Champion Slot Winners\n\n🏆 Winners from Wart’s Great Escape were announced and rewards were distributed.\n🎉 BossBoppa and Guppy93Allan claimed the Champion Slots, with the community thanked for strong participation.",
